# Copy to .env.local and adjust. .env.local is gitignored. README.md explains every setting.

# The wiki list normally lives in the config file, not here: config.json in your user config folder
#   macOS    ~/Library/Application Support/wiki-renderer/config.json
#   Linux    $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wiki-renderer/config.json, else ~/.config/wiki-renderer/config.json
#   Windows  %APPDATA%\wiki-renderer\config.json
# {"wikis": [{"id": "notes", "name": "Notes", "root": "~/notes/wiki"}], "printFileTitle": false}
# It is re-read when it changes (no restart). A relative `root` resolves against the file's own folder (WIKI_DIRS
# entries resolve against the repo's working directory). Deleting the file empties the list. WIKI_RENDERER_CONFIG names another file.
# WIKI_RENDERER_CONFIG=/path/to/config.json
#
# Developer override. When WIKI_DIRS is set the config file's wikis are ignored. Comma-separated `id=folder` pairs, or
# bare folders. A bare folder takes its id from the folder name (or the parent's, when the folder is called `wiki`).
# Ids are lowercase letters, digits and dashes, and unique. Relative paths resolve from this repo; `~/` from your home
# folder. With one wiki, / opens it; with several, / lists them. A bad value stops the server at startup.
# No default: this line is an example, point it at your own folder.
WIKI_DIRS=notes=~/notes/wiki
# Example with two wikis, ids `notes` and `project-management`:
# WIKI_DIRS=notes=~/notes,~/code/project-management/wiki

# Optional (code defaults shown).
# How often a request re-fingerprints a folder (stat only); edits show after this window.
# WIKI_RECHECK_MS=1000
# Total bytes one wiki may load into memory, attachments included (50 MiB). See "The size cap" in README.md.
# WIKI_MAX_BYTES=52428800
# How long a folder must have been unreadable before the reader shows the staleness notice.
# WIKI_SNAPSHOT_STALE_NOTICE_MS=0
# Hide Edit and refuse saves (the reader then never writes to a wiki folder).
# WIKI_READ_ONLY=false
# Print the heading made from a page's file name (no frontmatter title, no leading h1). The config file's
# printFileTitle sets it too; this variable wins when set.
# WIKI_PRINT_FILE_TITLE=false
# debug under `npm run dev`, info under `npm start`.
# LOG_LEVEL=debug

# ── Branding (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults: "Wiki Renderer" / "Wikis", a "WR" TenantLogo on the indigo ground, tab titles ending "· Wiki Renderer".
# BRAND_NAME=Wiki Renderer
# BRAND_PRODUCT=Wikis
# One or two letters; derived from BRAND_NAME when unset.
# BRAND_INITIALS=WR
# The ground behind the initials: indigo (default), deep or glow (design system v31 TenantLogo).
# BRAND_TONE=indigo
# An image file (png, jpg, svg, webp) shown instead of the initials. Unset by default; example:
# BRAND_LOGO=/path/to/logo.png
# The tab-title suffix; BRAND_NAME when unset, so tab titles end "· Wiki Renderer".
# BRAND_TITLE=Wiki Renderer
# Example of your own: BRAND_TITLE="The Firm Wikis"
